## A clear glass sphere before a two-tone backdrop, red left of x = 1 and blue right of it. The
## edge lies off the sphere's axis, so the sphere's index decides which colour a pixel inside it
## sees. The light reaches the backdrop alone and no shadow ray crosses the sphere. Kd 0.01 keeps
## interreflection, which only the path tracer renders, below the tolerance the test measures; the
## light makes up the radiance. Not third-party.
Display "glassparams_sphere.tif" "file" "rgba"
Format 64 48 1
PixelSamples 2 2
Option "pathtracer" "integer samples" [128]
Projection "perspective" "fov" [40]
Clipping 0.5 50
Translate 0 0 5
WorldBegin
LightSource "distantlight" 1 "from" [0.8 0.5 -0.33] "to" [0 0 0] "intensity" [260]
AttributeBegin
Surface "matte" "Kd" [0.01]
Color [1 0 0]
Polygon "P" [-12 -12 15  1 -12 15  1 12 15  -12 12 15]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
Surface "matte" "Kd" [0.01]
Color [0 0 1]
Polygon "P" [1 -12 15  12 -12 15  12 12 15  1 12 15]
AttributeEnd
AttributeBegin
Surface "glass"
Sphere 1.5 -1.5 1.5 360
AttributeEnd
WorldEnd
